sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Hiring Manager (CLI/Streamlit)
    participant A as matching_agent.py (LangGraph)
    participant T as tools.py (@tool wrappers)
    participant C as mcp_client.py (MCPClient)
    participant FS as filesystem_mcp_server.py
    participant IX as resume_index_mcp_server.py
    participant D as data/, reports/ (disk)

    Note over A,FS: process boundary -- subprocess, JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio

    U->>A: job description (text or file path)
    A->>C: get_fs_client()
    C->>FS: spawn subprocess + {"method":"initialize"}
    FS-->>C: serverInfo + capabilities

    rect rgb(235,245,255)
    Note over A,D: parse_jd
    A->>C: read_file(jd_path)
    C->>FS: {"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"read_file",...}}
    FS->>D: fs_tools.read_file() (path checked against allowed_roots)
    D-->>FS: text + metadata
    FS-->>C: {"result":{"content":[{"json":{...}}]}}
    C-->>A: jd_text
    end

    A->>T: extract_requirements(jd_text)
    T-->>A: must-have / nice-to-have skills

    A->>T: search_resumes(jd_text)  (Milestone 2 RAG, unchanged)
    T-->>A: initial_pool (Round 1)

    rect rgb(235,245,255)
    Note over A,D: rank_candidates (Round 2)
    loop each candidate in initial_pool
        A->>C: read_file(candidate.resume_path)
        C->>FS: tools/call read_file
        FS->>D: full resume text
        FS-->>C: text
        C-->>A: gaps + improvement_suggestions
    end
    end

    rect rgb(235,245,255)
    Note over A,D: generate_report (Round 3)
    A->>C: write_file(report_path, markdown)
    C->>FS: tools/call write_file
    FS->>D: fs_tools.write_file()
    FS-->>C: {"message":"File written successfully",...}
    C-->>A: confirmation
    end

    rect rgb(255,245,230)
    Note over A,IX: bonus: multi-MCP -- a second, independent server
    A->>C: get_index_client()
    C->>IX: spawn subprocess + initialize
    A->>C: call_tool("index_stats", {})
    C->>IX: tools/call index_stats
    IX-->>C: {"chunks_indexed": N}
    end

    A-->>U: report + interactive chat (interrupt/resume loop)
